comments.body:
[A10] Closure on the maintainer decision of 2026-09-06 (milestone 1 closes on simulation and CI quality; the booted-board remainder of this issue moves to milestone 3 under its owners).

A read-only verification of the eight acceptance boxes against dev 7fd04d45 (the merge of PR #371) found boxes 1 to 7 satisfied with fresh gate runs and hosted evidence, and box 8 partial:

- build surface: `--software-profile` accepts only `baremetal`, `--flashboot` only `none|baremetal`; both sweep recipes carry the bare-metal profile;
- removal: 170 tracked paths deleted in the #294 lane (59ba6ffb..40a2192a); six retired-stack paths at 59ba6ffb, zero at HEAD; generated text is scanned;
- documentation: REQUIREMENTS.md section 1 and DOC_GENERATION.md describe only the bare-metal product; docs_check 0 findings; retired files recoverable with `git show 59ba6ffb:<path>`;
- #110/#116/PR #228 reconciled on 2026-08-26; the option-OFF door is verification-only and refused elsewhere by the gate;
- `scripts/check_baremetal_only.py --check`: 0 findings across 758 files; `--selftest`: 336 arms PASS, with empty, missing and unreadable inventories exiting 2;
- hosted at 7fd04d45: docs 34056859720, elaborate 34056859560, rtl-fast 34056859544, rtl-full 34056859527 all green; `scripts/xvlog_gate.py --check` at the ratchet;
- booted board (2026-09-06, PR #361 head image, VERSION 0x00020057, AEM CRC e825b108): startup, UART, identity, AEM, fabric enabled, clock-validity owner and PHC proven after two cold cycles.

The body's acceptance section now carries the ticked boxes with their evidence, and the three open lines of box 8 are listed with their owners: gPTP lock on the bench wire is #358 (with #117 for the two-board evidence), power-cycle persistence on the booted image is #70, and audio datapath operation once the controller and capture hosts are back is #117. None of them is a Linux-removal property, so this issue closes on its subject.
